q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.487 Tw (Then she went home, opened the shoebox, and took out the first notebook and the last one. She) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 750.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (put them in her purse.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (The next day, she asked to speak to Vincent Castellano.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 692.02 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.534 Tw (He received her in the back office of a restaurant that did not have a name on the door. He was) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 671.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.700 Tw (smaller than she expected, up close. A man in his sixties with soft hands and a gold watch, the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 651.20 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.507 Tw (kind of man who had other people do his violence for him. He looked at her the way he looked) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 630.79 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (at furniture.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 601.31 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("You have something of mine," Elena said, and she set the first notebook on his desk.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 571.83 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.315 Tw (He opened it. His face did not change. He turned three pages, and his face did not change. Then) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 551.42 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.062 Tw (he reached the page with the date of Marco's death, and the name of the man who had ordered it,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 531.01 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (and the amount that had been paid for it, and his face changed completely.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 501.53 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Where did you get this?" he asked.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 472.05 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.707 Tw ("I served you coffee for ten years," Elena said. "You never looked at me. That was your) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 451.64 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (mistake.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 422.16 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.565 Tw (She laid out her terms, and they were simple. Danny's debt was gone, erased, forgotten. The) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 401.75 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.231 Tw (diner, the building it stood in, and the block around it would be transferred into her name within) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 381.35 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.372 Tw (the week. And Vincent Castellano would never send a man to her door again, because if he did,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 360.94 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.972 Tw (the remaining thirty-nine notebooks would go to a federal prosecutor whose name was written) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 340.53 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (on the very last page, in the very last notebook, in Elena's own handwriting.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 311.05 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.706 Tw (Vincent Castellano stared at her for a long time. Then he laughed, a short surprised sound, and) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 290.64 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (said, "Your husband taught you well.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 261.16 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("No," Elena said. "My husband taught me to be afraid. You taught me not to be.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 231.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.879 Tw (The debt vanished the next morning. The paperwork for the diner arrived on Friday. Danny) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 211.27 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.894 Tw (never played poker again. And Elena Ruiz still works the five a.m. shift, because she likes the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 190.86 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.468 Tw (quiet hour before the city wakes up, and because booth six is hers now. The men still come.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 170.45 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (They still talk. And Elena still writes it all down.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 140.97 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (She has forty-one notebooks. She is working on the forty-second.) Tj ET Q
BT /F3 12.00 Tf ET
q BT 65.20 111.49 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.268 Tw (If this story gave you goosebumps, the next one is even darker. A gardener spent thirty years) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 91.08 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (planting roses for a crime boss -- and burying something else underneath them. Read it next.) Tj ET Q
